- My name's Paul Mescal.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.548
- And this is love letters...
- Love letters.

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:08.258
- Love Letters from Letterboxd.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:10.635
- A little love. A little love
right there. Ooh.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:11.845
Little mood change.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.559
- I'm going to open this up

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:21.104
and find out what
this letter says.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.315
“Best 103 minutes of my life.” Wow.

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:26.568
- “I think it's safe to say

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:28.528
that all was quiet
in my living room

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.196
after watching this masterpiece.”

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:31.406
You are too kind.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:33.825
- “I love the songs.
Crying face.”

00:00:34.743 --> 00:00:36.786
But I'm having a
smiling face here.

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.873
- “We as a culture must
let Paul Mescal dance.”

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.043
He's probably referencing the “Under Pressure” sequence

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.545
with some questionable
dad dancing.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.171
And I agree.

00:00:46.171 --> 00:00:48.423
I feel like we as a culture
must let me dance

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:49.549
even though I'm not
that good at it.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.175
- “Heck, yeah.

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.385
I saw “Top Gun: Maverick”
in theaters

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.345
for a third time
and I'd do it again.

00:00:54.596 --> 00:00:56.681
This time was laser
focused on the editing of

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:58.266
Eddie Hamilton and
Chris Lebenzon.

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:00.226
Those two guys kept it tight.”

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:01.644
Thank you very much.
That's awesome.

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:02.395
- “Naatu naatu

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.190
naatu naatu, naatu naatu, naatu naatu

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.275
Pauses to wrestle a tiger and shoot a gun.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:09.611
Naatu naatu, naatu naatu, naatu.

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:10.653
Thank you very much.

00:01:10.653 --> 00:01:16.409
- “That f wolf was
terrifyingly hot.”

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.161
This person saying
the wolf is hot

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.580
is not the only
person saying that.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.041
- “The real star was
Angela Bassett's hair.”

00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:24.959
I'm sure Camille will love that.

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:27.962
- “The real star was
Angela Bassett’s hair.”

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.297
I like that one.

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:31.591
It was a such a transition
from the first one 

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.884
where she had the long locks.

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:35.804
And I'm just so happy that people loved it and enjoyed it.

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:38.348
- “Here's the beautiful thing
about all of this.

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.600
Todd Field has no interest
in easy answers.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.519
“TÁR” is a movie
that trusts the intelligence

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.522
of its viewers, that demands
attention to detail and wants

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:48.024
to start a discussion rather than tell you what to think

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:48.900
or how to feel.”

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.818
Thank you Marianna.

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:52.570
Well, Letterboxd is a big part of our cinematic life.

00:01:52.695 --> 00:01:55.657
Something that I read
quite a bit

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.325
and that I feel like I learn from.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:02:00.245
- “A twisty turny tale
with a sharply written script

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:02.205
and featuring Daniel Craig

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:04.624
in what seems to be
his favorite role.

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:07.043
“Glass Onion” was a
ton of fun.”

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:08.378
Oh, Deirdre!

00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:12.048
He is having a ton of fun
when he plays Benoit Blanc,

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:13.758
and that means it's
a good environment on set.

00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:15.635
That means everyone's
having a good time and

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.970
that's what we want.

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:18.805
- “I know Michelle Yeoh
was going to give

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:22.183
an amazing performance, which she absolutely did,

00:02:22.183 --> 00:02:24.477
but it was Ke Huy Quan who stole the show.

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:29.399
The innocence in his character,
and at the same time,

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:32.610
the badass version of his character is portrayed

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.489
brilliantly by him.
He was terrific.”

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.159
All the kindness that you all have shown me 

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.577
has really warmed my heart.

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:43.121
You have made this a really
emotional journey for me,

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:44.914
so I thank you
from the bottom of my heart.

